  "pages": [
    { "idx": 0, "label": "1", "overlay": 0, "note": "[45s] **Welcome.** This is the title slide.\n\nThe clock starts when you leave this page, like pdfpc. Press **?** for all keys." },
    { "idx": 1, "label": "2", "overlay": 0, "note": "[105s] The audience window opens with the deck; in the Mac app, behind this one. If the browser blocked it, press **o**.\n\n- **Shift+W** here puts it fullscreen on the projector (Chrome, Edge, the Mac app)\n- Otherwise drag it to the projector and double-click it" },
    { "idx": 2, "label": "3", "overlay": 0, "note": "[60s] Three reveal steps share one page label, so they count as **one slide**.\n\n*Next* on the right shows the next slide, not the next step." },
    { "idx": 3, "label": "3", "overlay": 1, "note": "[40s] Step two of three. A step can take its own time." },
    { "idx": 4, "label": "3", "overlay": 2, "note": "[50s] Last step. Going back from the next slide jumps to the first step." },
    { "idx": 5, "label": "4", "overlay": 0, "note": "[90s] Press `l` for the laser, and again to turn it off (`2` and `1` work too, as in pdfpc).\n\n`+` and `-` resize the laser while it is on." },
    { "idx": 6, "label": "5", "overlay": 0, "note": "[120s] 各位老师好，这一页的备注是中文。备注字号可以用 `+` 和 `-` 调整，`[` 和 `]` 调整当前幻灯片的大小。\n\n[ref] A note opening with its length, like `[120s]`, is the time planned for it. It's drawn as the lines under the slides instead of shown here." },
    { "idx": 7, "label": "6", "overlay": 0, "hidden": true, "note": "You only see this slide through the overview, the thumbnails or `g`." },
    { "idx": 8, "label": "7", "overlay": 0, "note": "[60s] The end slide: the talk is planned to end here, and backup slides follow." },
    { "idx": 9, "label": "8", "overlay": 0, "note": "[30s] Backup material, after the end slide. Its line runs against its own 30 s; the talk's clock keeps going, so early/late counts the detour." }
  ]
}
